1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,658
This video covers three helpers that make a site easier to build and to use:

2
00:00:05,658 --> 00:00:09,861
the Wizard, which guides visitors through a form one step at a time;

3
00:00:09,861 --> 00:00:14,121
Recipes, which set up a site from a ready-made script; and the shared

4
00:00:14,121 --> 00:00:16,620
resources that other screens build on.

5
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:24,582
A long form with dozens of boxes puts visitors off.

6
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:29,360
Splitting it into steps, with progress shown, gets more of them to the end.

7
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:34,907
Setting up the same content types, roles and settings by hand on every

8
00:00:34,907 --> 00:00:39,010
new site is slow, and each site ends up slightly different.

9
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:43,879
Screens also need the same small widgets again and again, such as a

10
00:00:43,879 --> 00:00:47,772
date range menu or a phone box with flags, and they should look

11
00:00:47,772 --> 00:00:49,860
and behave the same everywhere.

12
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:56,011
The Wizard, Recipes and the shared resources answer one problem each, so you

13
00:00:56,011 --> 00:00:57,790
build once and reuse.

14
00:01:01,990 --> 00:01:06,495
A wizard asks a visitor for information one step at a time, remembers

15
00:01:06,495 --> 00:01:11,300
the answers between steps, and creates content items from them at the end.

16
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:16,263
A recipe is a ready-made setup that you run from the admin.

17
00:01:16,263 --> 00:01:21,190
It creates content types, settings, roles or sample content in one go.

18
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:27,312
The shared resources are the common scripts and styles that other CrestApps screens

19
00:01:27,312 --> 00:01:32,140
use, so a date range menu or a phone box behaves the same in every module.

20
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:36,849
You build a wizard in the admin and run recipes from the admin.

21
00:01:36,849 --> 00:01:40,980
The shared resources need nothing from you except to be turned on.

22
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:48,920
A wizard is a content type that has the Wizard part.

23
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:55,277
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the type that will host the wizard.

24
00:01:55,277 --> 00:01:57,807
Here it is Workshop Registration.

25
00:01:58,259 --> 00:01:59,796
Click Add Parts.

26
00:01:59,796 --> 00:02:01,752
Wizard is in the list.

27
00:02:01,752 --> 00:02:03,849
Click Add and Configure.

28
00:02:04,305 --> 00:02:08,870
Contained content types are the kinds of step a wizard can have.

29
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:12,196
Choose Visitor Details and Visit Preferences.

30
00:02:12,196 --> 00:02:16,305
Each step is an ordinary content type with its own boxes.

31
00:02:16,755 --> 00:02:21,246
Requires an authenticated user is off, so anyone can take part.

32
00:02:21,246 --> 00:02:23,393
Tick it to require sign-in.

33
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:28,014
Completion policy decides what happens to the answers at the end:

34
00:02:28,014 --> 00:02:32,309
create and publish them, create drafts, or do not keep them.

35
00:02:32,309 --> 00:02:33,025
Save.

36
00:02:37,215 --> 00:02:39,666
Now create a Workshop Registration.

37
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:42,475
Give it a title, such as Spring workshop.

38
00:02:42,926 --> 00:02:49,201
Use Add step to add one card for each step, here Visitor Details and Visit Preferences.

39
00:02:49,201 --> 00:02:54,396
Each card holds that step's boxes, which can start with default values.

40
00:02:54,847 --> 00:02:58,159
The order of the cards is the order of the steps, and you

41
00:02:58,159 --> 00:02:59,998
can drag a card to change it.

42
00:02:59,998 --> 00:03:01,207
Publish the item.

43
00:03:05,399 --> 00:03:08,258
A link on your site sends visitors to the wizard.

44
00:03:08,258 --> 00:03:11,585
It opens on the first step, with a progress bar at the top

45
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:13,249
that shows where they are.

46
00:03:13,701 --> 00:03:17,104
The visitor fills in the first step and clicks Next.

47
00:03:17,104 --> 00:03:20,801
The progress bar marks it done, and the answers are kept.

48
00:03:21,251 --> 00:03:27,541
On the second step, Previous goes back without losing anything, and Finish completes the wizard.

49
00:03:27,992 --> 00:03:31,112
A confirmation page tells the visitor it is done.

50
00:03:35,285 --> 00:03:41,907
With the completion policy on create and publish, each step's answers are now content items.

51
00:03:41,907 --> 00:03:48,125
Open Content, Content Items, and find the Visitor Details and Visit Preferences items.

52
00:03:52,314 --> 00:03:53,920
Open Tools, Recipes.

53
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,206
Recipes are grouped by feature.

54
00:03:56,206 --> 00:04:00,530
Each one has a name, tags, and a description of what it creates,

55
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:02,754
so you know before you run it.

56
00:04:03,217 --> 00:04:07,119
Type in the Search box to find a recipe by name or tag.

57
00:04:07,119 --> 00:04:11,277
Run starts a recipe and reports the result when it is done.

58
00:04:11,729 --> 00:04:13,998
Recipes can also be pasted in.

59
00:04:13,998 --> 00:04:16,708
Open Tools, Deployments, JSON Import.

60
00:04:16,708 --> 00:04:21,561
The editor suggests the steps and their settings as you type, and marks

61
00:04:21,561 --> 00:04:23,829
mistakes before anything runs.

62
00:04:28,029 --> 00:04:32,409
The date range menu offers presets such as Last 7 Days or This

63
00:04:32,409 --> 00:04:35,566
Month, and a custom range, in one dropdown.

64
00:04:35,566 --> 00:04:37,369
Report filters use it.

65
00:04:38,119 --> 00:04:41,859
The phone box with a country flag picker is shared by the Phone

66
00:04:41,859 --> 00:04:44,839
Field and by screens that ask for a phone number.

67
00:04:45,589 --> 00:04:51,915
Select-all checkboxes on admin lists, collapsible panels, date and time pickers and item

68
00:04:51,915 --> 00:04:54,809
selectors are shared in the same way.

69
00:04:55,559 --> 00:05:00,046
Because they come from one place, every screen looks and behaves the same,

70
00:05:00,046 --> 00:05:04,869
and they are turned on once, together with the CrestApps features that use them.

71
00:05:09,069 --> 00:05:14,539
Event or workshop registration that asks for details in a few short steps.

72
00:05:15,289 --> 00:05:21,359
Customer onboarding, with one step for contact details and another for preferences.

73
00:05:22,109 --> 00:05:29,019
A recipe that creates the same content types, roles and sample pages for every new site.

74
00:05:29,769 --> 00:05:35,769
A recipe for a training or demo site, run again whenever you need a fresh copy.

75
00:05:37,769 --> 00:05:41,805
Build a wizard once to guide visitors step by step, run a recipe

76
00:05:41,805 --> 00:05:45,552
to set a site up in one click, and let the shared resources

77
00:05:45,552 --> 00:05:47,570
keep every screen consistent.

78
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:49,069
Thanks for watching.

